Done. Here is the record.

## Decision (CD-8, IN-CONTRACT)

The contract requires `start` to record a `pid` but does not say whose. I decided: **the recorded pid is the run's lifetime marker — by default the parent of the `start` invocation (the dispatcher shell that will observe the exit code), with `--pid=N` for a dispatcher that knows the run's own pid.** `status` never reads a log; it reads that pid. `getmypid()` of `start` would be dead immediately (the exact false signal in reverse), so the parent is the honest default; explicit `--pid` stays available because the dispatcher is the only party that truly knows. All paths used were in `allowed_scope`; no scope addition was needed.

