## The instrument, demonstrated (real output, real exit codes)

**Classification matrix** (temp ledger, real tool invocations; `finish` exited `0` each time):
```
demo-failed      failed     exit=1   log=0B report=0B
demo-silent      silent     exit=0   log=0B (/tmp/ledger-demo/zero.log)
   NOTE: exit 0 with no report/log content — a silent success...
demo-completed   completed  exit=0   log=0B report=7592B (.ai/ai-autonomy-mechanise-doctrine.flash-run.log)
```

**`abandoned` reconciliation** (recorded `running` before, dead pid, `status` persisted `abandoned`):
```
recorded status before status: running
  demo-abandoned   abandoned  exit=-  age=0s  pid=2109729 ...
GATE: BLOCKED — demo-failed, demo-silent, demo-abandoned      >> status --gate exit=3
recorded status after reconciliation: abandoned
```
Live pid stays `running`; `--gate` exits `3` while silent/failed/abandoned exist, `0` when every run is clean (`GATE: OK`). `status --json --gate` also exits `3`. Default `.ai/runs` is empty → `status --json` exit `0`, `--gate` exit `0`.

**`claims` on the real 7,592-byte report** — every claim `unverified`, and the tool states re-derivation is a later slice:
```
